 ## MVP Scope
 
@@ -98,11 +98,13 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Queue lifecycle:** queues are managed by `App\Actions\CreateQueue` (owner/admin only, slug defaults to `Str::slug($name)`, unique per `(entity_id, slug)`) and `App\Actions\UpdateQueue` (owner/admin only, rename with the same uniqueness rule, toggle `is_active`). There is **no delete surface** — removal = `is_active = false`; tickets are history and remain intact, while `IssueTicket` / `CallNextTicket` reject inactive queues via `InactiveQueueException`.
 
-**Queue access:** employees operate only queues with a `queue_access` grant row (`permissions` JSON, MVP vocabulary `call` only via `App\Enums\QueuePermission`). Grants are managed by `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess` (owner/admin only, target membership and queue must share the entity, empty list revokes, audited to the `audit` channel). Owner/admin call without a grant row; non-members are denied everywhere. Authorization lives in `App\Policies\QueuePolicy` (`create`/`update`/`manageAccess`/`call`) and is enforced server-side inside the domain actions, not only at future HTTP/Livewire callers.
+**Queue access:** employees operate only queues with a `queue_access` grant row (`permissions` JSON, MVP vocabulary `call` only via `App\Enums\QueuePermission`). Grants are managed by `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess` (owner/admin only, target membership and queue must share the entity, empty list revokes, audited to the `audit` channel). Owner/admin call without a grant row; non-members are denied everywhere. Authorization lives in `App\Policies\QueuePolicy` (`create`/`update`/`manageAccess`/`call`) and is enforced server-side inside the domain actions, not only at HTTP/Livewire callers.
+
+**Web panels:** `App\Livewire\Entity\Queues` (owner/admin) lists, creates, renames and deactivates queues and manages employee `call` grants; `App\Livewire\Entity\Serve` is the attendant panel available to any member, with callable-queue filtering, the three call modes, a 30-ticket waiting preview and rate-limited call-next. Both resolve every client-supplied id scoped to the current entity and delegate writes to the domain actions above.
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation. HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation. The Livewire queue-management and serve panels are the current HTTP layer for these rules; TV/display and real-time broadcasting remain future work.
 
